  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two thermodynamical process are shown in the figure. The molar heat capacity for process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>. The molar heat capacity at constant pressure and constant volume are represented by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></math>, respectively. Choose the correct statement.</p><img src=\"assets\\qt0028_7fc53dd52b17.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 256px;\"/>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>∞</mo></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\qt0028_7fc53dd52b17.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 256px;\"/></p><p>For process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi><mi>log</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo></math> Constant</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>V</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo> </mo><mo>…</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Likewise, for process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>→</mo><mi>P</mi><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo></math> Constant</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mo>…</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Also, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi><mo> </mo><mo>…</mo><mfenced><mi>iii</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>By <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>iii</mi></mfenced></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></math></p>"
  }
}